+/// tip
+
+For most cases, you can now simply use `yield` in your *path operation function* to stream data, without creating a `StreamingResponse` yourself. Read more about it in [Stream JSON Lines](../tutorial/stream-json-lines.md){.internal-link target=_blank}.
+
+Use `StreamingResponse` directly when you need full control over the response, for example to set a custom media type or headers.
+
+///
+
 /// note | Technical Details
 
 An `async` task can only be cancelled when it reaches an `await`. If there is no `await`, the generator (function with `yield`) can not be cancelled properly and may keep running even after cancellation is requested.
